# An approval's command rows (`.prd/tui-phase4` T10): fx cuts a command with
# `CommandSegmentIterator` (`approval_ui.zig:265-340`) over its terminal-safe
# text (`projectCommandText`, `:228-247`), not with the composer's wrap. Two
# commands, each refused with `3`: A's lines are aimed at 116 cells (120
# columns less `  $ `), B's at 76 (80 less it) -- a word that ends at the
# margin after a space (it goes down), an escape token across the margin (it
# goes down whole), and, in A only, an OSC 8 link, wide glyphs and a tab made
# inert, an empty line, a token longer than a row, three spaces across the
# margin, and a trailing line break. B is its first two lines, so that xfx's
# band -- which also says what `2` would grant, and asks only what fits --
# can ask it at 24 rows. The tools are each product's own: fx's `shell` is
# xfx's `terminal`.
fx: gateway cmd-wrap-fx.json
xfx: gateway cmd-wrap-xfx.json
fx: seed approvals-fx-settings.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
wait 10
type run the two commands
wait 2
key Enter
wait 20
snap cmd-a
key 3
wait 20
snap cmd-b
key 3
wait 20
snap after
snapfull after
